### Fractional Commodity Ledger — runnable from IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client).
### Run them top to bottom. After "Create user", set @userId to the returned id.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@userId = 1

### List commodities
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/commodities
Authorization: Basic trader trader123

### Create user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Basic trader trader123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Reeck Demo", "email": "reeck.demo@example.com" }

### Deposit INR 10,000
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/wallet/deposit
Authorization: Basic trader trader123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10000 }

### Buy INR 2,000 of GOLD (wallet 10,000 -> 8,000)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trades/buy
Authorization: Basic trader trader123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "commodity": "GOLD", "amount": 2000 }

### Buy 0.5 g of SILVER with an idempotency key (send twice: second reply has "replayed": true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trades/buy
Authorization: Basic trader trader123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "commodity": "SILVER", "quantity": 0.5, "clientOrderId": "silver-order-001" }

### Portfolio
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Authorization: Basic trader trader123

### ADMIN: change GOLD price
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/commodities/GOLD/price
Authorization: Basic admin admin123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pricePerUnit": 13000 }

### Sell INR 1,040 of GOLD
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/trades/sell
Authorization: Basic trader trader123
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": {{userId}}, "commodity": "GOLD", "amount": 1040 }

### Trade history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/trades
Authorization: Basic trader trader123

### Ledger history of the user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/ledger
Authorization: Basic trader trader123

### ADMIN: verify ledger integrity
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ledger/verify
Authorization: Basic admin admin123
